WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:05.572
Step one evaluates Microsoft Learn's
two service account decision tables,

3
00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:10.601
from Securing on-premises service
accounts and Securing cloud-based service

4
00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.773
accounts, exactly as
published: twelve tests pass,

5
00:00:13.773 --> 00:00:16.713
and the thirty-one not
run are the example's own.

6
00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:20.948
Step two lists what the matrix
needs: two read permissions, License

7
00:00:20.948 --> 00:00:25.724
Assignment dot Read dot All and User dot
Read dot All, and only the GET method.

8
00:00:25.724 --> 00:00:30.413
Step three runs Modules 1 and
2 quietly, then the matrix.

9
00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:34.945
Twenty-one identities are in scope
and twenty get a proposal: six retire,

10
00:00:34.945 --> 00:00:39.631
seven keep, two group managed and two
delegated managed service accounts,

11
00:00:39.631 --> 00:00:43.088
two managed identities, and
one federated credential.

12
00:00:43.088 --> 00:00:46.141
The owners have decided
eighteen of twenty-two,

13
00:00:46.141 --> 00:00:49.587
in two waves, and each wave
holds one high-risk account.

14
00:00:49.587 --> 00:00:55.112
The license decision is Tier 1, two in
scope, and the tenant holds two units.

15
00:00:55.112 --> 00:00:58.662
Seven findings, four warnings,
one information item.

16
00:00:58.662 --> 00:01:01.020
And the last line: Gate 2 is not met,

17
00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.820
with the open findings for
each of its five criteria.
